@prefix delphi: <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/> .

sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/favored-fixation-lower-bound> dct:description "Proof scope of Fixation is at least i/M when selection does not oppose the mutant: 3 statement(s) the Lean kernel checked and 3 assumption(s) stated in the module header and not proved." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: For any absorbing chain on {0..M} copies with E[X_{t+1} | X_t = i] >= i (stochastic, both ends absorbing, positive one-step escape from every interior state), P(fixed by t) is nondecreasing and bounded, its limit u(i) exists, and u(i) >= i/M (Delphi.FavoredChain.fixationProbability_ge); also u(i) <= 1." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: Wright-Fisher sampling with success probability (1+s) i / (M + s i), s >= 0, is such a chain (Delphi.wrightFisherSelection), so a single new mutant fixes with probability at least 1/M." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: The defined expected count M mu u T equals mu T for the neutral Wright-Fisher chain, is at least mu T for any favored chain, and is at most M mu T for any u <= 1." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: The expected count is a DEFINITION (rate x generations, independent fates, Kimura 1968); linkage, interference, changing M, changing s and overlapping generations are excluded by it, not shown absent." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: Selection enters only through the sampling probability (1+s) i / (M + s i), constant in time and across sites." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: mu, T, M are free parameters; the module measures nothing. Which mutations are favored, how many a trait needs, and in what order, are outside it." ;
    rdfs:comment "The kernel-checked statements are theorems of the model; the assumptions are the model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Favored.lean> .
}

sub:provenance {
  sub:assertion prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-lean-thread-builder> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Favored.lean> , <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-lean-thread-builder> a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "delphisci lean thread (Claude Fable 5.1 writing the Lean modules and this builder; the Lean kernel, not the model, checked the proofs)" ;
    delphi:usesModel <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a delphi:LanguageModel ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1" ;
    dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" .
}

